the human immunodeficiency virus  commonly known as HIV is a retrovirus  that causes acquired immunodeficiency  syndrome or AIDS this is a condition  that causes the progressive failure of  the immune system by allowing  life-threatening infections to thrive  recently new gene therapy methods using  HIV have been created to cure cancer  this involves creating modified HIV the  HIV is created by taking out the  proteins that would cause the HIV to  remain harmful when essential protein in  the survival of HIV is the HIV one  matrix protein p17 as it participates in  the early stages of reproduction for the  virus by removing this protein HIV can  no longer successfully reproduce in the  host cell this is an animation of the  p17 protein by modifying the HIV it is  no longer dangerous and can no longer  affect patients as it would if normal  HIV was used SMAW defied HIV can then be  inserted into healthy t-cells which are  white blood cells that are procured from  the patient normally t-cells cannot  detect cancer cells an antigen is  necessary for normal T cells to become  activated the leftover genetic material  from the modified HIV can help these new  tumor and infiltrating lymphocytes or  TILs to easily recognize an antigen  found on cancerous cells this antigen is  a surface protein cd19 the TILs function  as serial killer T cells and target the  cancer cells quickly and effectively  this is an animation of the CV 19  protein and a photo of the TILs locating  and killing the cancerous cells in a  patient once the special T cells are  infused into the blood there is cellular  war the TI ELLs go from one tumor cell  to the next  and kill them eventually the cancer will  be gone though a newly developed  treatment the combination of HIV and  cancer could be the gateway to the cure  for cancer  you
 

